**Biograph** (shipped here as *fossibleHIS*, repo `fossibleworks/biograph`) is an open-source hospital information system (HIS). It is a fork of Marley Health with extra features, built as a **Frappe app named `healthcare`** that adds a healthcare domain to **ERPNext**. Most of its data model follows **HL7 FHIR**.

**Who uses it:** clinics, hospitals and individual practitioners. That covers front-desk and registration staff, physicians, nurses, lab and diagnostic technicians, therapists, billing and insurance staff, and patients. Patients use the Vue patient portal at `/patient-portal` and the web forms.

**Main areas** (see `healthcare/modules.txt` and the workspace sidebars `healthcare`, `outpatient`, `inpatient`, `diagnostics`, `rehabilitation`, `insurance`, `setup`):
- Patient management, including configurable duplicate-patient checks
- Outpatient care: practitioner schedules, Patient Appointment (slot-based and block-time booking, recurring appointments, practitioner unavailability), Patient Encounter, Fee Validity
- Inpatient care: Inpatient Record, admission and discharge, service unit occupancy billing, Inpatient Medication Orders and Entries
- Clinical Procedures, Service Requests and Medication Requests
- Laboratory and diagnostics: Lab Test, Sample Collection, Observation, Diagnostic Report
- Rehabilitation and physiotherapy: Therapy Plan, Therapy Session, Exercise Types
- Insurance: payor contracts, patient insurance policies and coverage, claims
- Medical coding: Code System, Code Value and Codification Table, moving toward FHIR terminology parity
- Regional: India ABDM integration (`healthcare/regional/india`)

Billing, accounts, stock and pharmacy, HR and assets come from ERPNext. Biograph hooks into ERPNext doctypes such as Sales Invoice, Payment Entry and Company.

The license is GNU GPL v3.
